From d4c4bd8431510b2fb46445c5d5ee1e99307cd0bb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: joinalahmed <joinalahmed@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 11:34:58 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Build max_unpool on BuildScatterShlo and route the non-out
 variants through the out variant

Addresses the review on #6105:

- The lowering reshapes self and indices to [B, S_in] and calls
  BuildScatterShlo(zeros[B, S_out], dim=1, ..., ScatterOp::kReplace) instead
  of assembling the ScatterOp and its dimension numbers by hand.
- ValidateMaxUnpoolInputs returns absl::Status and ComputeOutputDimensions
  returns the output shape, built with ConcreteSizeToDimensions.
- MaxUnpoolOut writes into `out`; AtenMaxUnpool{2,3}d allocate an empty
  tensor and call it. The explicit resize is gone from the dispatch path,
  which DispatchOpOut resizes itself; it stays on the zero-size path, which
  assigns the buffer directly.
- NumElements from error_utils.h replaces the hand-rolled products.
- Input dtype is validated: ValidateNotLowPrecisionFloat, then a
  floating-point check, since ATen's max_unpool kernels are only implemented
  for floating-point inputs (bool, integer, complex and float8 all fail with
  "not implemented" on CPU). Covered by
  test_max_unpool2d_non_floating_point_input.

Assisted-by: Claude Fable 5.1
